{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Deck Plus 3-1/2-inch screws felt relevant because I recently chose long outdoor wood screws; their length and intended use are close to what I have needed.",
    "The PRIMESOURCE 3-inch construction screws fit my recent interest in general wood fastening, and the one-pound box feels practical to try."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "BOSTITCH flooring nails do not meet the same need as my framing nails. Sharing a brand and a similar length does not make them suitable for the same job or equipment.",
    "The 1-1/4-inch wood screws are substantially shorter than my recent choices, so being wood screws alone is not enough to make them useful now.",
    "The kerosene can, cutting wheels, plumbing supplies, storage bags and epoxy each require a specific need I have not expressed. I would not choose them simply because they could be useful around a workshop."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My fastening purchases seem to have been interpreted as interest in a broad range of maintenance and workshop supplies.",
    "Shared brands and broad product names seem to matter too much when the actual fastening purpose and dimensions differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The length and intended use of my recent wood screws matter: long outdoor or construction screws are more relevant than much shorter screws.",
    "My nail purchases specify framing use, collation and dimensions; another type of nail needs to match the task and equipment before I would consider it.",
    "My occasional purchases of medicine cups and vacuum bags reflect separate needs, rather than an ongoing desire for unrelated supplies."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in wood fastening, but stretched it into unrelated supplies and overlooked important differences in length, purpose and equipment compatibility."
}"}
